WEBVTT

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:11.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the twenty-fourth. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.310
<v Marcus Hale>Bit tinny, but yeah, you're there.</v>

00:00:17.089 --> 00:00:19.890
<v Priya Raman>Fine this end. Think it's your speaker, Marcus.</v>

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:27.620
<v Hannah Price>Before we start, did anyone watch the football last night? Honestly, that last ten minutes.</v>

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.109
<v David Whitfield>Turned it off. Apparently that was the sensible decision.</v>

00:00:32.219 --> 00:00:37.119
<v Hannah Price>Wish I had. Sat there arguing with the telly like it could hear me.</v>

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:41.039
<v Sarah Okafor>So, much like a Teams call, then.</v>

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:49.090
<v Marcus Hale>I'm supposed to be going walking at the weekend. Looking at the weather, it'll be swimming instead.</v>

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:52.590
<v Tomasz Nowak>It's only Tuesday. Forecast will change six times.</v>

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.670
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, from rain to heavy rain. We've booked somewhere now, anyway.</v>

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.600
<v Jamie Brennan>Optimistic. Very unlike you.</v>

00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:07.010
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the weather forecast—Callum Reid's absent today. Everyone else is on.</v>

00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:12.069
<v David Whitfield>Yep, I'm here. Camera's off, but I am actually here.</v>

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:15.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Updates from yesterday first?</v>

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:25.250
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, the shift handover report I was going to send round—can that move to stores Jamie? Jamie, can you take the sending round off me?</v>

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:31.290
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll take that over from you and send the shift handover report round.</v>

00:01:33.269 --> 00:01:34.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, thanks both.</v>

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:40.489
<v Jamie Brennan>And the new starters' training records, I've sorted those. All fine, that's done.</v>

00:01:42.719 --> 00:01:45.519
<v Hannah Price>Lovely. Nice to hear 'all fine' for once.</v>

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:54.430
<v Jamie Brennan>Tomasz asked me to pass on the monthly fire alarm test as well. That's stuck—the contractor can't get here until it's rescheduled.</v>

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Ah, right. Understood.</v>

00:01:56.739 --> 00:02:04.790
<v Tomasz Nowak>And, um, I've made a start on the risk assessment update. Got into it, but there's a fair bit left to work through.</v>

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:09.289
<v David Whitfield>Always more boxes than space to write in, those forms.</v>

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>Paperwork doesn't have a bypass, unfortunately.</v>

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.039
<v Sarah Okafor>If only. Anything else before the new stuff?</v>

00:02:19.009 --> 00:02:24.610
<v Jamie Brennan>Just a finished one: finished the repair on the Water Booster Pump last night. That's sorted.</v>

00:02:26.259 --> 00:02:30.110
<v Marcus Hale>Lovely. Not the most generous corner for getting your hands into.</v>

00:02:30.719 --> 00:02:33.870
<v Jamie Brennan>Designed by someone with much smaller knuckles than mine.</v>

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:41.099
<v Priya Raman>Oh, and I heard a slight rattle from the long belt. Just an observation, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:47.409
<v David Whitfield>Could you hear it over the general racket, or only close up?</v>

00:02:48.919 --> 00:02:52.069
<v Priya Raman>Only close up. Very faint, no more than that.</v>

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, just an observation for now.</v>

00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:01.110
<v Tomasz Nowak>Half the trick in there is knowing which rattle you're listening to.</v>

00:03:02.919 --> 00:03:11.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, new work. We need to swap the filter on the CT1 by the end of the week. And that one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.400
<v Marcus Hale>Have we actually got anyone available to take that?</v>

00:03:17.699 --> 00:03:21.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't take it on, sorry. Haven't got the capacity.</v>

00:03:21.539 --> 00:03:26.439
<v David Whitfield>No, nor me. Don't want to say yes and then leave it sitting there.</v>

00:03:26.909 --> 00:03:29.360
<v Priya Raman>I can't pick that one up either.</v>

00:03:30.969 --> 00:03:35.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. It needs doing, but we've got nobody taking it at the moment.</v>

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:39.330
<v Jamie Brennan>I can't offer to do that from stores, I'm afraid.</v>

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:44.280
<v Sarah Okafor>No, understood. I'm not going to pretend it's covered.</v>

00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:48.139
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah. That's a gap, then.</v>

00:03:49.449 --> 00:03:51.900
<v Sarah Okafor>It is. Okay, the other new one.</v>

00:03:53.330 --> 00:04:02.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, can you book a contractor to look at the GT2 water valve? Need that booked by tomorrow at 9:30. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:03.259 --> 00:04:10.610
<v Hannah Price>Yeah—sorry, just checking, tomorrow at 9:30 is when you need the booking sorted, not when they need to be standing here?</v>

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:16.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, the booking sorted by tomorrow at 9:30. That's the deadline.</v>

00:04:17.699 --> 00:04:24.350
<v Hannah Price>Fine, I'll book a contractor to look at the GT2 water valve and have the booking sorted by then.</v>

00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:26.829
<v David Whitfield>Yep, makes sense.</v>

00:04:27.949 --> 00:04:31.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. That's the new work covered in the discussion, then.</v>

00:04:33.889 --> 00:04:39.839
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry if there's a load of banging coming through. It's the door behind me, not anything exciting.</v>

00:04:41.569 --> 00:04:44.370
<v Priya Raman>I thought someone was applauding the meeting finishing.</v>

00:04:45.589 --> 00:04:47.339
<v Marcus Hale>Wouldn't put it past them.</v>

00:04:48.079 --> 00:04:50.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheeky. Right, thanks everyone. We'll leave it there.</v>

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.490
<v Jamie Brennan>Cheers, all.</v>
